  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Africa Regional (Africa: C&#xF4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire, Liberia, Sierra Leone): Mano River Union Trafficking In Persons (MRU-TIP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Targeted Trafficking in Persons (TIP) focal points in Mano River countries have harmonized legal and policy frameworks to combat TIP. 2) TIP task forces of the targeted Manor River Union countries have the knowledge and tools required to monitor, analyze and report TIP information. 3) Targeted law enforcement and justice actors know the requirements of their respective TIP acts, action plan and standard operating procedures.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: The MRU Secretariat, the TIP Secretariats in the three (3) targeted countries, the Judiciary and Legal Training Institute and the Police Training School of Sierra Leone, Justice sector actors (investigators, prosecutors and judges) in the three (3) targeted countries, the Liberia Female Law Enforcement Agency, and women law enforcement associations in Sierra Leone.Indirect beneficiaries: Population of the MRU countries.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to ensure that Mano River Union countries work more effectively together to investigate, prosecute and adjudicate human trafficking cases.</narrative>
  </description>
